/** This is a file detailing the release history of TRW. It is
 ** arranged in reverse chronological order, ie, the first entry
 ** is the most recent, the last entry is the least recent. That
 ** way, the more recent, and supposedly the most interesting
 ** changes are outlined first in the file and you don't have to
 ** mess around with the old stuff to see what I'm up to.
 */

0.1.5        9  3 94     Public Beta Release

         o  While searching for bugs and changing some file I/O
            around, managed to dress up and tighten some code a
            bit.  Executable is a bit more compact.

         o  Much file I/O has been changed over to asynchronous
            mode.  This greatly speeds up the file area loading,
            although it doesn't seem to boost the save speed as
            much as I wanted.  The biggest boost is in the file
            area copy routine -- which is the primary target.

            *** NOTE ***

            This increases the stack requirement of the
            executable to 40K.

         o  Enforcer hit reported in file area redirection
            requester.  Was addressing this routine with a
            ulong instead of a short (if that means anything to
            you).  Appears to have been banished.

         o  Ocasionally, moving or copying file areas would
            cause the file pointers to get mangled.  Tough
            bug to trace, but eventually I was able to both
            duplicate it and then stomp it (I think).

0.1.4        8 20 94     Private Version

         o  File Templates partially enacted, but halfway through
            received word of several bugs that really needed my
            attention more.  Templates scrubbed temporarilly.

0.1.3        7 30 94     Public Beta Release

         o  A few complaints about the behavior of the File Area
            Manager's File Area display were taken into account
            and modification was made. Before, the list would
            atomatically position the selected area at the top of
            the list, now it remains as is.

         o  Version string bug fixed.  TRW now contains embedded
            version information that can be displayed via
            AmigaDOS "Version" or a similar program, if desired.

         o  All windows now bear close gadgets, which work.  In
            most cases, these cause the program to quit. In a few
            cases, they back you out of a requestor or whatever
            (it should be obvious where at, let me know if not).

         o  Added gadgets to the main screen to solve the file
            area lockout dilemma. Now, you cannot enter the file
            area manager if the current file area has users in
            it. To get around this, a gadget showing the current
            file area, the number of users in it, and a button
            allowing selection of a different file area have been
            added to the main screen.

         o  Changed things around a little bit as far as the look
            and feel of TRW goes. Also should have a minor GUI
            bug solved, but to do so I had to have borders on
            everything. Win some, lose some.

         o  Implemented PRINT REPORT function in File Area
            Manager.  Will print to either a file or to the
            printer.

0.1.2                Public Beta Release  (Bug fix!)

         o  AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAARRRRRRRRGH!!!!!!!!!!

            In case you missed it, I introduced a HIDEOUS bug
            into TRO 0.1.1 that would cause TRW to fail BADLY
            when adding a new file area.  It would try to get a
            lock on the new file area before saving the file area
            to FILE:AREA.BBS.  ICK ACK ACK ACK!

         o  Reduced code size a bit AND made the code slicker by
            using the DLG.Library Inform() function to inform
            users of new file areas.

0.1.1                Public Beta Release

         First working release.  File Area Manager ONLY is
         active, the rest of the program is disabled.  Most
         functions in the file area manager are "hot."  Be warned
         NOW!

         o  Added code to put up a busypointer while TRW is doing
            things of great import, to indicate that it's not wise
            to mess with it yet.

         o  Added code to exclusively lock a file area away from
            the users while you're messing with them.

         o  Added SIGS button for editing file SIGs.

         o  Added MERGE AREAS button.  This will allow sysop to
            merge two file areas together.  Thanks to Scottie
            Swenson for the suggestion.

         o  Added Fido Config button that will allow sysop to
            configure his/her favorite TICK program's config file
            from the same place as everything else is done.

         o  Added Print Report button to print a report on all
            file areas.

         o  Removed RATIOS box from the file area manager.  It
            will re-appear at a more appropriate place.

         o  Removed EDIT FILES and FILES status gadget from the
            File Area Manager.  Not appropriate for the planned
            function of the file area manager.

         o  Rearranged all gadgets to take advantage of the file
            area manager's real estate.

         o  Changed the functionality of the user global file
            management to reduce the size of the code and make it
            a bit more sane to look at (for me).  8-)

         o  Measures taken to reduce the flickering effect
            noticed by many testers.

0.06      6 26 94    Visual Beta Release

         Nasty font-related bug reported from many sites. It
         appears the font-adaptive code in GadToolsBox 2.0 isn't
         as adaptable as it seems, or else I misunderstand it.

0.05      6 20 94    Visual Beta Release

         First public release with most code disabled or not yet
         implemented. Released to find out if the interface is
         valid before I get hip deep into code.

